  "description": "For the application with ID\u202f7b8c9d0e1f2a3b4c5d6e7f8a, the integration inventory shows two configured integrations on page\u202f1 (10 results per page) out of a total of 20. The view is filtered to show only records where\u202fenabled:true (filter field\u202fenabled) and the results are sorted by\u202fname\u202fin ascending order.\n\nThe first entry is the Google Pub/Sub integration (ID\u202f5f2c1e3a9b4d6f0a1b2c3d4e, integration ID\u202f6a3b4c5d6e7f8a9b0c1d2e3f) created on\u202f2023\u201108\u201101T12:34:56Z and last updated on\u202f2023\u201109\u201115T08:22:10Z. It belongs to the same application (ID\u202f7b8c9d0e1f2a3b4c5d6e7f8a) and is currently\u202fenabled. The integration is named \u201cGoogle Pub/Sub Integration\u201d and its type is\u202fgooglePubSub. It publishes to the topics\u202fprojects/my-gcp-project/topics/topic1\u202fand\u202fprojects/my-gcp-project/topics/topic2. Its Google Pub/Sub configuration specifies the project ID\u202fmy-gcp-project and the service\u2011account credentials JSON:\n\n\"{\\\"type\\\":\\\"service_account\\\",\\\"project_id\\\":\\\"my-gcp-project\\\",\\\"private_key_id\\\":\\\"abcdef1234567890\\\",\\\"private_key\\\":\\\"-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----\\\\nMIIEv...\\\\n-----END PRIVATE KEY-----\\\\n\\\",\\\"client_email\\\":\\\"service-account@my-gcp-project.iam.gserviceaccount.com\\\",\\\"client_id\\\":\\\"12345678901234567890\\\",\\\"auth_uri\\\":\\\"https://accounts.google.com/o/oauth2/auth\\\",\\\"token_uri\\\":\\\"https://oauth2.googleapis.com/token\\\",\\\"auth_provider_x509_cert_url\\\":\\\"https://www.googleapis.com/oauth2/v1/certs\\\",\\\"client_x509_cert_url\\\":\\\"https://www.googleapis.com/robot/v1/metadata/x509/service-account%40my-gcp-project.iam.gserviceaccount.com\\\"}\".  \n\nIts status reports a last keep\u2011alive timestamp of\u202f1694800000, a next retry scheduled for\u202f1694810000, a successful connection recorded at\u202f1694800000, and no recent disconnect (timestamp\u202fnull, error\u202f\u201c\u201d).\n\nThe second entry is an MQTT device integration (ID\u202f8c9d0e1f2a3b4c5d6e7f8a9b, integration ID\u202f9d0e1f2a3b4c5d6e7f8a9b0c) created on\u202f2023\u201107\u201120T09:15:30Z and last updated on\u202f2023\u201109\u201110T14:45:00Z. It also belongs to application\u202f7b8c9d0e1f2a3b4c5d6e7f8a but is currently\u202fdisabled. The integration is titled \u201cMQTT Device Integration\u201d with type\u202fmqtt, and it subscribes to the topics\u202fsensors/temperature\u202fand\u202fsensors/humidity. Its MQTT configuration includes client ID\u202fmqtt-client-001, username\u202fuser123, password\u202fpass123, a clean session flag set to\u202ftrue, port\u202f8883, protocol\u202fmqtts, and host\u202fmqtt.example.com. The security material is supplied as follows: private key\u202f\"-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----\\\\nMIIEv...==\\\\n-----END PRIVATE KEY-----\", certificate\u202f\"-----BEGIN CERTIFICATE-----\\\\nMIID...==\\\\n-----END CERTIFICATE-----\", and CA certificate\u202f\"-----BEGIN CERTIFICATE-----\\\\nMIID...==\\\\n-----END CERTIFICATE-----\".  \n\nStatus for this integration shows a last keep\u2011alive at\u202f1694700000, the next attempt scheduled for\u202f1694710000, a connection timestamp of\u202f1694700000, and a recent disconnect at\u202f1694705000 with the error message \u201cConnection timeout\u201d."
